{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"function useThrottledCallback<TFn>(fn, options): (...args) => void;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/preact-pacer/src/throttler/useThrottledCallback.ts#L43","children":[{"type":"text","value":"throttler/useThrottledCallback.ts:43"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A Preact hook that creates a throttled version of a callback function.\nThis hook is essentially a wrapper around the basic "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"throttle"},{"type":"text","value":" function\nthat is exported from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/pacer"},{"type":"text","value":",\nbut optimized for Preact with reactive options and a stable function reference."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The throttled function will execute at most once within the specified wait time period,\nregardless of how many times it is called. If called multiple times during the wait period,\nonly the first invocation will execute, and subsequent calls will be ignored until\nthe wait period has elapsed."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This hook provides a simpler API compared to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useThrottler"},{"type":"text","value":", making it ideal for basic\nthrottling needs. However, it does not expose the underlying Throttler instance."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For advanced usage requiring features like:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Manual cancellation"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Access to execution counts"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Custom useCallback dependencies"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Consider using the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useThrottler"},{"type":"text","value":" hook instead."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tfn","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TFn"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFn"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"extends"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AnyFunction"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"fn","children":[{"type":"text","value":"fn"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFn"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/PreactThrottlerOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"PreactThrottlerOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFn"},{"type":"text","value":", {\n}>"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"(..."},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"args"},{"type":"text","value":") => "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"void"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// Throttle a window resize handler\nconst handleResize = useThrottledCallback(() => {\n  updateLayoutMeasurements();\n}, {\n  wait: 100 // Execute at most once every 100ms\n});\n\n// Use in an event listener\nuseEffect(() => {\n  window.addEventListener('resize', handleResize);\n  return () => window.removeEventListener('resize', handleResize);\n}, [handleResize]);","lang":"tsx"}],"headings":[{"id":"type-parameters","text":"Type Parameters","level":2},{"id":"tfn","text":"TFn","level":3},{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"fn","text":"fn","level":3},{"id":"options","text":"options","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2},{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction useThrottledCallback<TFn>(fn, options): (...args) => void;\n```\n\nDefined in: [throttler/useThrottledCallback.ts:43](https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/preact-pacer/src/throttler/useThrottledCallback.ts#L43)\n\nA Preact hook that creates a throttled version of a callback function.\nThis hook is essentially a wrapper around the basic `throttle` function\nthat is exported from `@tanstack/pacer`,\nbut optimized for Preact with reactive options and a stable function reference.\n\nThe throttled function will execute at most once within the specified wait time period,\nregardless of how many times it is called. If called multiple times during the wait period,\nonly the first invocation will execute, and subsequent calls will be ignored until\nthe wait period has elapsed.\n\nThis hook provides a simpler API compared to `useThrottler`, making it ideal for basic\nthrottling needs. However, it does not expose the underlying Throttler instance.\n\nFor advanced usage requiring features like:\n- Manual cancellation\n- Access to execution counts\n- Custom useCallback dependencies\n\nConsider using the `useThrottler` hook instead.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TFn\n\n`TFn` *extends* `AnyFunction`\n\n## Parameters\n\n### fn\n\n`TFn`\n\n### options\n\n[`PreactThrottlerOptions`](../interfaces/PreactThrottlerOptions.md)\\<`TFn`, \\{\n\\}\\>\n\n## Returns\n\n(...`args`) => `void`\n\n## Example\n\n```tsx\n// Throttle a window resize handler\nconst handleResize = useThrottledCallback(() => {\n  updateLayoutMeasurements();\n}, {\n  wait: 100 // Execute at most once every 100ms\n});\n\n// Use in an event listener\nuseEffect(() => {\n  window.addEventListener('resize', handleResize);\n  return () => window.removeEventListener('resize', handleResize);\n}, [handleResize]);\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: useThrottledCallback\ntitle: useThrottledCallback\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction useThrottledCallback<TFn>(fn, options): (...args) => void;\n```\n\nDefined in: [throttler/useThrottledCallback.ts:43](https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/preact-pacer/src/throttler/useThrottledCallback.ts#L43)\n\nA Preact hook that creates a throttled version of a callback function.\nThis hook is essentially a wrapper around the basic `throttle` function\nthat is exported from `@tanstack/pacer`,\nbut optimized for Preact with reactive options and a stable function reference.\n\nThe throttled function will execute at most once within the specified wait time period,\nregardless of how many times it is called. If called multiple times during the wait period,\nonly the first invocation will execute, and subsequent calls will be ignored until\nthe wait period has elapsed.\n\nThis hook provides a simpler API compared to `useThrottler`, making it ideal for basic\nthrottling needs. However, it does not expose the underlying Throttler instance.\n\nFor advanced usage requiring features like:\n- Manual cancellation\n- Access to execution counts\n- Custom useCallback dependencies\n\nConsider using the `useThrottler` hook instead.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TFn\n\n`TFn` *extends* `AnyFunction`\n\n## Parameters\n\n### fn\n\n`TFn`\n\n### options\n\n[`PreactThrottlerOptions`](../interfaces/PreactThrottlerOptions.md)\\<`TFn`, \\{\n\\}\\>\n\n## Returns\n\n(...`args`) => `void`\n\n## Example\n\n```tsx\n// Throttle a window resize handler\nconst handleResize = useThrottledCallback(() => {\n  updateLayoutMeasurements();\n}, {\n  wait: 100 // Execute at most once every 100ms\n});\n\n// Use in an event listener\nuseEffect(() => {\n  window.addEventListener('resize', handleResize);\n  return () => window.removeEventListener('resize', handleResize);\n}, [handleResize]);\n```\n"}
